#
# Straight-line depreciation, in Sutra (neap_rules.h NR3): what period
# `period` of an asset's life of `life` periods is charged, in minor units:
# (cost - salvage) / life truncated as COMPUTE does (the floor: nothing
# here is negative) in every period but the last, and in the last what
# is left, so the charges sum to cost - salvage exactly. cost and salvage
# fit 9(12); base (cost - salvage), most (1200 - life), left (life -
# period) and first (period - 1) are unsigned, so a salvage past the cost,
# a life past 1200 periods or a period outside 1..life is a size error and
# a life of 0 a division Sutra refuses. straight.tb takes a cost to 15
# digits: past 12 the two disagree, held.
record neap-straight
  cost: 9(12)
  salvage: 9(12)
  life: 9(4)
  period: 9(4)
  base: 9(12)
  most: 9(4)
  left: 9(4)
  first: 9(4)
  each: 9(12)
  charge: 9(12)
procedure
  compute base = cost - salvage
  compute most = 1200 - life
  compute left = life - period
  compute first = period - 1
  compute each = base / life
  if left > 0
    answer each
  end-if
  compute charge = base - each * (life - 1)
  answer charge
